## Frequently Asked Questions

### Do I need a primary care physician referral to see a therapist with HealthSpring?

Referral requirements depend on your specific plan structure. HMO plans frequently require a primary care physician referral prior to seeing a specialist, whereas PPO plans generally allow direct scheduling. Always check your specific plan details with Cigna HealthSpring.

### Does Cigna HealthSpring cover online therapy in Texas?

Yes. Most Cigna Medicare Advantage plans include coverage for telehealth mental health sessions when delivered through secure platforms, making therapy convenient for residents across Texas.

### What should I do if a therapist is out-of-network with my HealthSpring plan?

If a clinician is out-of-network, you may choose to pay for services out-of-pocket. If you have a PPO plan, the practice can supply a monthly superbill for you to submit to your insurer for potential out-of-network reimbursement.

### How much does an outpatient counseling session cost with Medicare Advantage?

In-network copays for outpatient therapy under Medicare Advantage typically range between $10 and $40 per session after any applicable deductibles have been satisfied. Exact rates depend on your plan's specific summary of benefits.

## Conclusion

Understanding your insurance coverage is an empowering step toward prioritizing your mental health. By verifying your plan details and identifying compatible care options, you can access effective, professional support without financial surprises.\
